# PR / Push Hygiene (lessons from #350)

Hard gates in [30-pre-push-ci-gates.mdc](30-pre-push-ci-gates.mdc) and
[31-pr-repo-guards-checklist.mdc](31-pr-repo-guards-checklist.mdc) still apply.
This rule adds failure modes that repeatedly blocked merge.

## 1. Serial edit → format → test → commit

Never commit while parallel file edits on the same package are unfinished.

```text
Edit → gofmt → go test <actual touched packages> → commit -s → push
```

Example (substitute the packages you changed):

```powershell
gofmt -w packages/revocation services/proxy/internal/auth
go test ./packages/revocation/... ./services/proxy/internal/auth/...
git commit -s -m "..."
git push origin HEAD
```

A missing import pushed mid-edit wastes a CI cycle.

## 2. After every push: PR head must equal branch tip

```powershell
git branch --show-current
git status -sb   # confirm upstream tracking
git push -u origin HEAD
$tip = git rev-parse HEAD
$head = gh pr view <N> --json headRefOid -q .headRefOid
# require $tip -eq $head before watching CI
# if still mismatched after a successful push: escalate (do not invent close/reopen workarounds first)
```

Do not watch CI until `headRefOid == HEAD`.

## 3. CodeScene scores `*_test.go` too

- No near-duplicate assert helpers (>~10 similar lines) — one parameterized helper
- No multi-clause `if a || b || c` in tests — extract single-condition helpers
- Same limits as prod: ≤40 lines/fn, nesting ≤3, ≤4 params (`21-complexity-management.mdc`)

## 4. SCA even on Go-only PRs

`ci-gate-security` still scans `pnpm-lock.yaml`. Before opening/updating a PR:

```powershell
# preferred if installed:
osv-scanner --lockfile pnpm-lock.yaml
# or avoid drive-by web dep churn; bump next if advisory hits
```

## 5. Resolve conversations before merge

Branch protection requires conversation resolution. Green checks ≠ mergeable.

```powershell
# unresolved review threads must be 0:
gh api graphql -f query='
query($n:Int!) {
  repository(owner:"Rick1330", name:"ibex-harness") {
    pullRequest(number:$n) {
      reviewThreads(first:100) { nodes { isResolved } }
    }
  }
}' -F n=<N> --jq '[.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved==false)] | length'
# want 0; then:
gh pr view <N> --json mergeStateStatus -q .mergeStateStatus   # want CLEAN
```

## 6. Design self-review before first push (auth / cache / security)

- Fail closed on ambiguous upstream results
- Concurrent structures race-tested
- Metrics series materialized at init (no first-hit registration)
- No raw tokens / secrets in logs
- Redis / pub-sub failures must not fail durable Postgres mutations
